ploys approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $308K ranks in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $834 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Centuri Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $2.1B market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 8% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $8M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 550% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.497482970814956},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Utilities peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Growing faster than most Utilities peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Centuri Holdings (CTRI) A Bargain As Earnings Rebound?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-ctri/centuri-holdings/news/is-centuri-holdings-ctri-a-bargain-as-earnings-rebound","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965285.355,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.588,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the CTRI Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Responsive_Playbooks_and_the_CTRI_Inflection_110526065402_1793922842.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793922842.0,"origin":"tiingo","senti